there is some startling news from the  centers for disease control this morning  the agency says as many as  215 000 more people than usual  died in the u.s during the first seven  months of the year it suggests the  number of lives lost to the coronavirus  is significantly higher than the  official toll  a review of the data by the ap and the  marshall project  finds that half of the people who died  were people of color  it comes as the u.s death toll from  covid 19 exceeds 175  thousand the pandemic is forcing schools  to adjust  and readjust their plans to reopen for  the fall semester  michael george is in brooklyn new york  this morning michael good morning  dana good morning schools just reopened  but already we're seeing outbreaks at  multiple campuses across the country  now a lot of parents teachers and  students are anxious about a return to  the classroom  moving into college may quickly become  moving out  thanks to unsanctioned gatherings by  students many putting  fun over safety  crowd scenes posted on social media  frustrated health professionals  and fellow students i hoped that as  college students we could have been  responsible enough to maybe keep this  from happening  17 students were suspended at st olaf's  college in minnesota for partying off  campus  president david anderson wrote students  and parents this is the kind of reckless  behavior that will put an  end to our in-person semester and it  must stop  eight students have tested positive 50  are quarantined  syracuse university suspended 23  students  for crowding into the campus quad this  week at notre dame in indiana  336 confirmed covet cases were reported  leading to a plea in the student  newspaper don't make us write obituaries  but the debate over safety isn't limited  to universities  before takeoff jet blue passengers in  orlando florida had their own  bumpy ride as a flight attendant told  the mother of a two-year-old to put a  mask on the child  though she and her six children did not  continue on to newark  others who flew were delayed 53 minutes  jetblue said its policy is for  passengers over the age of two to wear  masks in accordance with cdc air travel  guidelines  and masks hard to spot at this alabama  high school football game  are required we're telling the people if  there's an outbreak there won't be high  school football  all this as the cdc warns americans need  to get their flu shots  this year more than ever  schools here in new york are set to  reopen in three weeks even as the  teachers union is raising the red flags  over safety concerns  they say if their concerns are not  addressed they'll go to court  or even strike jeff michael thank you  very much
 

